# Flatpack UI conventions

Flatpack is our Rails view component library. It provides UI components and CSS themes. The Recording Studio ecosystem uses Flatpack exclusively. Gem, dummy, and Admin screens should use Flatpack components.

- Gem: https://github.com/bowerbird-app/flatpack
- Public demo: https://flatpack.bowerbird.io/

Use Flatpack components for new UI whenever an appropriate component exists. Before creating a component, custom CSS, or hand-rolled UI markup, search for an existing Flatpack component and inspect established usage in this repository. Prefer composing Flatpack components over duplicating their HTML or styling.

Do not recreate buttons, forms, alerts, cards, modals, navigation, or other design-system elements with custom markup or CSS. Semantic layout markup is acceptable when Flatpack does not provide the required structure.

If you find custom CSS or UI that could use ViewComponents Flatpack already provides, update those screens. If you need a component Flatpack does not provide, ask whether to create a custom component or update Flatpack. Explain the gap before introducing a custom implementation.

Do not automatically rewrite unrelated legacy UI merely because it appears in a touched file. When modifying legacy UI, migrate the affected element to Flatpack when the change is local and behavior can be preserved safely.
